# NotebookLM ↔ Cursor

## Notebook

- **Name:** `Global_Retirement_ETF_Strategy`
- **URL:** https://notebook.google.com/notebook/e9ef0d28-6b83-41ca-889b-14f23078c8bc
- **ID:** `e9ef0d28-6b83-41ca-889b-14f23078c8bc`

MCP server: `notebooklm` (`npx -y notebooklm-mcp@latest` in `~/.cursor/mcp.json`). First use requires Google login in the MCP browser window; fully quit/relaunch Cursor after changing MCP config.

**Auth gotcha:** if Google redirects to `notebook.google.com` but the MCP waiter only watches `notebooklm.google.com`, login never “completes.” Use CLI auth that accepts both hosts (details in `docs/notebooklm.md`). Live Q&A for this notebook has been verified authenticated.

## When to call NotebookLM MCP

- Synthesize across many uploaded sources (skill + memos + research playbooks)
- Pull citation-backed summaries already refined in the notebook (allocation guide, checklist, standing prompts)
- Cross-check a proposal against the notebook’s distilled notes before writing a long memo

## When NOT to call NotebookLM

- **Live fund figures** (TER, AUM, duration, yield): verify from issuer factsheets; date-stamp or write `n/v`. Never treat NotebookLM as the authority for numbers that change.
- **File placement / repo layout:** follow `AGENTS.md`
- **Day-to-day ETF analyst behavior:** follow `src/retirement-etf-analyst/SKILL.md` (+ its `references/`)

## Conflict resolution

1. `src/retirement-etf-analyst/SKILL.md` (+ references) wins for analysis policy
2. `.cursor/rules/retirement-etf-brief.mdc` wins for durable portfolio constraints when MCP is offline
3. NotebookLM answers are synthesis aids — cite them, do not override the skill on conflicts

## Hygiene

- Do not commit Google cookies, MCP auth state, or `.env` secrets
- Keep this repo private; the notebook holds personal financial context
- After material portfolio memo changes under `data/processed/`, refresh the brief (see `docs/notebooklm.md`)
